<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-Tenders total A$105 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-Tenders total A$105 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australia commercial paper market has opened the week with promissory note issuance totalling A$105 million amid generally subdued short-end dealings.</p>
<p>North Ltd's sale of A$50 million worth of 30-day paper was the morning highlight, being the first issue from the miner's recently launched A$300 million domestic programme.</p>
<p>The notes went at 5.5 basis points over BBSW.</p>
<p>Dealers said short-end market torpor was due to dwindling fund manager interest in the almost flat physical bill curve.</p>
<p>At 0120 GMT (12.20 p.m.), June 90-day bank bill futures were up one point to 93.93.</p>
